Tile 1 — SQL Server Host CPU Usage (5 named SQL hosts)
timeseries cpu_pct = avg(dt.host.cpu.usage, scalar:true),
  by:{dt.entity.host},
  filter: dt.entity.host in [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | filter in(lower(entity.name), array(
        "pftwswifscq03.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifsq0101.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifscq03.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifsq0102.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifscq04.prd.hcscad.net"
      ))
    | fields id
  ]
| fieldsAdd hostname = entityName(dt.entity.host)
| fieldsAdd cpu_pct = round(cpu_pct, decimals:2)
| fields hostname, cpu_pct
| sort cpu_pct desc

Tile 2 — SQL Server Memory Usage in GB (Total / Used)
timeseries used_b  = avg(dt.host.memory.used, scalar:true),
           avail_b = avg(dt.host.memory.avail.bytes, scalar:true),
  by:{dt.entity.host},
  filter: dt.entity.host in [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | filter in(lower(entity.name), array(
        "pftwswifscq03.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifsq0101.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifscq03.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifsq0102.prd.hcscad.net",
        "pwauswifscq04.prd.hcscad.net"
      ))
    | fields id
  ]
| fieldsAdd hostname = entityName(dt.entity.host)
| fieldsAdd total_gib = round((used_b + avail_b) / 1073741824, decimals:1)
| fieldsAdd used_gib  = round(used_b / 1073741824, decimals:1)
| fieldsAdd used_pct  = round((used_b / (used_b + avail_b)) * 100, decimals:2)
| fields hostname, total_gib, used_gib, used_pct
| sort used_pct desc

🔍 Discovery — Blocking Sessions & Long-Running Queries (tenant-specific check needed)

Per your own metric catalog, sql-server.local.general.processesBlocked is the documented "blocked processes" metric ✅, and long-running queries would come from Query Store metrics (sql-server.queries.*) which are only 🟡 documented, not yet confirmed in your tenant . Let's verify both exist and are collecting for your 5 SQL hosts:

fetch metric.series
| filter contains(metric.key, "sql-server")
   and (contains(metric.key, "block") or contains(metric.key, "quer") or contains(metric.key, "lock"))
| summarize count(), by:{metric.key}
| sort metric.key asc


